[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 2"""
 date="2026-10-30T14:34:26Z"
 content="""
As far as I can see, core.worktree is the only config setting that
is relative to the path of the gitdir.

Changing the gitdir to be where the symlink points to does not seem like a
good idea, it would affect git-annex code that creates symlinks pointing
into the gitdir.

Also, `git rev-parse --git-dir` is just ".git" in this situation,
so even git internally does not follow the symlink manually, except
presumably when resolving core.worktree.

So, I've fixed this only in the core.worktree handling code in
updateLocation.
"""]]
